{
 "_about": "The Use Report and Search & Replace, one way for the Python Editor and the viewer's: run by tests/test_use_cases.py (EditorSession.uses, replace_plan, replace_uses, set_script_text; usesindex.index_rows; mwscript.rename.replace_id) and viewer-shell/editcore/tests/cases.rs (editcore::uses, editcore::rename, editcore::scripts). Each case is a load order (`plugins`, each with its masters and its records in the tes3conv schema, in file order) and operations: [\"uses\", tag, id], [\"plan\", tag, id, new id, cell or null] (what Search & Replace would change: {field: [tag, key, field, value]}, {ref: [cell, origin, index, changes]}, {new: [cell, label, fields]}), [\"replace\", tag, id, new id, cell or null] (editReplace's answer), [\"script_text\", id, text], [\"place\", cell, tag, id, translation], [\"index\", plugin] (the use index's rows), [\"rename\", text, old, new], [\"pending\"], [\"can_undo\"], [\"undo\"]. The script compiler is a stand-in on both sides: a script compiles unless its text says nocompile. A new reference's random editor name is given as a label (U1, U2, ...). `expect` is what each gave and the journal after them. Generated from the Python side when a case is added, and read by hand.",
